    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Central PVTGs vs. State PVTGs: Abujhmaria, Baiga, Birhor, Kamar, and Hill Korwa are designated by the Union Government, while Pando and Bhunjia are state-designated PVTGs.",
        "Leadership of Revolts: Gundadhur led the Bhumkal Revolt of 1910, while Gaind Singh led the Paralkot Rebellion of 1825.",
        "Tribal Shifting Cultivation: Note local terms like 'Bewar' (Baiga tribe) and 'Dahiya' (Gond sub-groups) for competitive exam questions."
      ],
